While main's coverage runs, let me plan the code changes. Let me review the areas to refactor:

### Fix 1: `mergeVerdictGate.runGate` (CC 13)

The thread suggests: "Extract the read→parse→resolve walk into a small helper (e.g. `effectiveVerdictOf(io, owner, name, inp, out)`) so `runGate` keeps only the short-circuit branches, and/or cover the remaining branches."

Current runGate structure (decision points):
1. `if (!out.head) return out;`
2. `if (!inp.logins || !inp.logins.length)` (2 branches)
3. try/catch around prCommentList (catch branch)
4. `if (!comments) return out;`
5. try/catch around latestVerdictForHead (catch branch)
6. `if (!effective) return out;`
7. `out.verdict = effective.record.verdict; if (!verdictHolds(...)) return out;`
8. `out.held = true; stampHold(...)`

Extract into `effectiveVerdictOf(io, owner, name, inp, out)`:
```js
function effectiveVerdictOf(io, owner, name, inp, out) {
   var comments;
   try {
       comments = prCommentList(io && io.getComments, owner, name, inp.prNumber);
   } catch (eRead) {
       out.commentsUnreadable = true; // fail-open
       return null;
   }
   if (!comments) return null; // capability miss — fail-open
   try {
       return reviewVerdicts.latestVerdictForHead(
           reviewVerdicts.parseVerdictRecords(coments, { authorLogins: inp.logins || [] }),
           out.head);
   } catch (eParse) {
       out.commentsUnreadable = true; // paranoia — the parser never throws
       return null;
   }
``
Then runGate:
```js
function runGate(io, owner, name, input) {
   var inp = input || {};
   var out = {...};
   if (!out.head) return out;
   if (!inp.logins || !inp.logins.length) return out;
   var effective = effectiveVerdictOf(io, owner, name, inp, out);
   if (!effective) return out;
   out.verdict = effective.record.verdict;
   if (!verdictHolds(out.verdict)) return out;
   out.held = true;
   stampHold(io, owner, name, comments?...)
``
Wait — stampHold needs `comments` for dedup. Currently: `stampHold(io, owner, name, comments, inp, out, effective.record)`. If effectiveVerdictOf returns only the effective verdict, runGate loses `comments`. Options:
- Return `{ effective, comments }` from the helper — an object; `if (!res || !res.effective)`. Hmm that adds branches.
- Or move stampHold INTO effectiveVerdictOf? No — keep the hold decision in runGate.
- Or: have effectiveVerdictOf return the effective record and stash comments in out? Hacky.
- Better: split differently — `verdictReadOf(...)` returns `{ comments, effective }` (or null on fail-open):

Actually cleanest: helper `readAndResolve(io, owner, name, inp, out)` returns `null` when the walk fails open, else `{ comments, effective }`. runGate:
```js
var found = readAndResolve(io, owner, name, inp, out);
if (!found) return out;
out.verdict = found.effective.record.verdict;
if (!verdictHolds(out.verdict)) return out;
out.held = true;
stampHold(io, owner, name, found.comments, inp, out, found.effective.record);
return out;
``
